WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.304
Ever wondered what's actually happening in a basketball game?

2
00:00:03.354 --> 00:00:05.930
Here's basketball, explained in two minutes.

3
00:00:06.959 --> 00:00:08.558
Two teams of five share one court,

4
00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.125
twenty-eight metres long.

5
00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:11.135
At each end is a hoop,

6
00:00:11.185 --> 00:00:13.354
three metres and five centimetres high.

7
00:00:13.663 --> 00:00:15.273
Put the ball through the other team's hoop.

8
00:00:15.323 --> 00:00:16.808
Most points wins.

9
00:00:17.854 --> 00:00:18.547
Know the court.

10
00:00:18.597 --> 00:00:20.813
The centre circle, where the game begins.

11
00:00:21.156 --> 00:00:23.442
The key, the painted area under the basket.

12
00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.678
The free-throw line.

13
00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:27.405
And the three-point arc, six point seven five metres

14
00:00:27.455 --> 00:00:28.742
from the basket.

15
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.193
Each team has five positions.

16
00:00:31.243 --> 00:00:32.890
The point guard runs the play.

17
00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:35.055
The shooting guard scores from range.

18
00:00:35.214 --> 00:00:37.604
The small forward does a bit of everything.

19
00:00:37.798 --> 00:00:39.942
The power forward and the centre battle near the

20
00:00:39.992 --> 00:00:41.047
basket.

21
00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:43.948
The game starts with a tip-off.

22
00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:45.399
The referee throws the ball up,

23
00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:47.327
and the two centres jump to tap it to

24
00:00:47.377 --> 00:00:48.594
a teammate.

25
00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:52.723
You move the ball by dribbling or passing.

26
00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:54.780
Take steps while holding the ball,

27
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.105
and that's travelling.

28
00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:58.061
Stop dribbling, then dribble again,

29
00:00:58.111 --> 00:00:59.607
and that's a double dribble.

30
00:00:59.981 --> 00:01:01.777
Break a rule, and the other team gets the

31
00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:02.743
ball.

32
00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:04.940
Now, scoring.

33
00:01:05.218 --> 00:01:07.153
A basket from inside the arc is worth two

34
00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:07.910
points.

35
00:01:08.954 --> 00:01:10.484
From behind the arc, three.

36
00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:13.744
And a free throw is worth one.

37
00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.570
Keep it moving.

38
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.962
The attack has eight seconds to cross halfway,

39
00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.949
and twenty-four seconds to shoot.

40
00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:23.903
Too slow, and the ball goes to the other

41
00:01:23.953 --> 00:01:24.845
team.

42
00:01:26.077 --> 00:01:28.327
On defence, stop them without fouling.

43
00:01:28.571 --> 00:01:29.556
Steal the ball.

44
00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:31.469
Block the shot.

45
00:01:32.327 --> 00:01:33.299
And when a shot misses,

46
00:01:33.349 --> 00:01:34.728
grab the rebound.

47
00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:39.571
Pushing, holding or hitting a player is a foul.

48
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.342
Foul a shooter, and they get free throws.

49
00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.770
Five personal fouls, and you're out of the game.

50
00:01:47.008 --> 00:01:49.247
A game has four quarters of ten minutes.

51
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.514
If the score is tied,

52
00:01:50.564 --> 00:01:53.395
play five minutes of overtime until there's a winner.

53
00:01:55.242 --> 00:01:56.272
That's basketball.

54
00:01:56.322 --> 00:01:57.688
Grab a ball, and we'll see you on the

55
00:01:57.738 --> 00:01:58.653
court.
